<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Constantine II of Scotland</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 952</span> · <a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a> · Also known as Causantín mac Áeda</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Constantine II was king of Alba, the kingdom that became <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scotland">Scotland</a>, from about 900 to 943, one of the longest reigns of early Scottish kings. He submitted to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aethelstan">Æthelstan</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eamont-bridge">Eamont Bridge</a> in 927 but joined the coalition defeated by Æthelstan at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-brunanburh">Battle of Brunanburh</a> in 937. He abdicated to become a monk at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/st-andrews">St Andrews</a> and died in 952.</p></div>
